{"files":[{"content":"#include<stdio.h>\n#include<stdlib.h>\n#include<string.h>\n#include<stddef.h>\n#include<stdint.h>\n\n/* Maximum size (in char) for neighbors and compute lists */\n#define MAX 100\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int id;\n  float value;\n  char neighbors[MAX];\n} Node;\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int *keys;\n  int *indices;\n  size_t capacity;\n} IdIndex;\n\n/* Reads input, allocates memory, writes graph size and node list. Returns the graph. */\nNode* read_input(char* fname, int *n, char* list) {\n  Node* data = NULL;\n  FILE *fl = NULL;\n\n  if (fname == NULL)\n    fl = stdin;\n  else\n    fl = fopen(fname, \"r\");\n\n  if (fl == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n\n  /* Keep the scanset on the current line; the leading space belongs to the list. */\n  list[0] = '\\0';\n  fscanf(fl, \"%d%99[^\\n]\", n, list);\n\n  if (*n > 0) {\n    data = (Node*) malloc ((*n)*sizeof(Node));\n    if(data == NULL){\n      fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n      exit(1);\n    }\n  }\n\n  for(int i = 0; i < *n; i++) {\n    data[i].neighbors[0] = '\\0';\n    fscanf(fl, \"%d %f%99[^\\n]\", &data[i].id, &data[i].value, data[i].neighbors);\n  }\n\n  fclose(fl);\n  return data;\n}\n\n/* Mix an integer ID before masking it into the power-of-two table. */\nstatic size_t hash_id(int id) {\n  uint32_t x = (uint32_t)id;\n  x ^= x >> 16;\n  x *= UINT32_C(0x7feb352d);\n  x ^= x >> 15;\n  x *= UINT32_C(0x846ca68b);\n  x ^= x >> 16;\n  return (size_t)x;\n}\n\n/* Build an open-addressed index; retaining the first occurrence matches the old scan. */\nstatic void build_id_index(IdIndex *index, const Node *g, int size) {\n  index->keys = NULL;\n  index->indices = NULL;\n  index->capacity = 0;\n\n  if (size <= 0)\n    return;\n\n  size_t max_size = (size_t)-1;\n  size_t count = (size_t)size;\n  if (count > max_size / 2) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n  size_t needed = count * 2;\n  size_t capacity = 1;\n  while (capacity < needed) {\n    if (capacity > max_size / 2) {\n      fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n      exit(1);\n    }\n    capacity *= 2;\n  }\n  if (capacity > max_size / sizeof(int)) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n\n  index->keys = (int*)malloc(capacity * sizeof(int));\n  index->indices = (int*)malloc(capacity * sizeof(int));\n  if (index->keys == NULL || index->indices == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n  index->capacity = capacity;\n\n  for (size_t i = 0; i < capacity; i++)\n    index->indices[i] = -1;\n\n  size_t mask = capacity - 1;\n  for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n    size_t slot = hash_id(g[i].id) & mask;\n    while (index->indices[slot] != -1 && index->keys[slot] != g[i].id)\n      slot = (slot + 1) & mask;\n    if (index->indices[slot] == -1) {\n      index->keys[slot] = g[i].id;\n      index->indices[slot] = i;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n/* Returns the first index of the node with the given ID, or -1 if absent. */\nstatic int find_by_id(const IdIndex *index, int id) {\n  if (index->capacity == 0)\n    return -1;\n\n  size_t mask = index->capacity - 1;\n  size_t slot = hash_id(id) & mask;\n  int found = index->indices[slot];\n  if (found == -1)\n    return -1;\n  if (index->keys[slot] == id)\n    return found;\n\n  slot = (slot + 1) & mask;\n  for (;;) {\n    int first_event = 4;\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#pragma omp simd reduction(min:first_event)\n#endif\n    for (int lane = 0; lane < 4; lane++) {\n      size_t candidate = (slot + (size_t)lane) & mask;\n      int candidate_index = index->indices[candidate];\n      int event = (candidate_index == -1 || index->keys[candidate] == id) ? lane : 4;\n      first_event = event < first_event ? event : first_event;\n    }\n\n    if (first_event < 4) {\n      size_t candidate = (slot + (size_t)first_event) & mask;\n      int candidate_index = index->indices[candidate];\n      return candidate_index == -1 ? -1 : candidate_index;\n    }\n    slot = (slot + 4) & mask;\n  }\n}\n\n/* Computes the sum for the node with the given id */\nfloat get_costly(Node *g, int id, const IdIndex *index) {\n  char *t;\n  int idmax = -1;\n  float max = 0;\n  char *auxptr;\n\n  int nd = find_by_id(index, id);\n  if(nd < 0)\n    return max;\n\n  char aux[MAX];\n  strcpy(aux, g[nd].neighbors);\n  t = strtok_r(aux, \" \", &auxptr);\n\n  while (t != NULL) {\n    int neighbor_id = atoi(t);\n    int d = find_by_id(index, neighbor_id);\n    if (d >= 0 && max < g[d].value) {\n      max = g[d].value;\n      idmax = neighbor_id;\n    }\n    t = strtok_r(NULL, \" \", &auxptr);\n  }\n\n  float r = g[nd].value;\n\n  if(idmax != -1)\n    r += get_costly(g, idmax, index);\n\n  return (r);\n}\n\n/* Main program - calls read input, computes sum for each node in the list, prints output */\nint main() {\n  char *fileN = NULL;\n  char computelist[MAX];\n  int n = -1;\n  Node* input = NULL;\n\n  input = read_input(fileN, &n, computelist);\n  IdIndex index;\n  build_id_index(&index, input, n);\n\n  // process\n  for(char *c = strtok(computelist, \" \"); c != NULL; c = strtok(NULL, \" \"))\n    printf(\"%s: %f\\n\", c, get_costly(input, atoi(c), &index));\n\n  free(index.keys);\n  free(index.indices);\n  free(input);\n  return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/graph.c"}],"hypothesis":"A scalar home-bucket check keeps the common lookup path cheap; when collisions continue, evaluating four consecutive probe candidates with an OpenMP SIMD minimum reduction may reduce branch-dependent lookup latency. Separate key and index arrays make the candidate fields contiguous. Selecting the earliest empty or matching slot preserves linear-probing order and first-match behavior.","notes":"This isolates changes to the ID index and find_by_id; recursive traversal, neighbor selection, and output remain unchanged. The SIMD directive is guarded by _OPENMP, with equivalent scalar code otherwise. No build or correctness measurements were run.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Split hash-table keys and node indices into contiguous arrays.","Retain a scalar check of the home bucket, then examine collision candidates in groups of four with an OpenMP SIMD min reduction to select the earliest match or empty slot."]}